From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] pastix.c: select the ordering with PASTIX_ORDERING

ccx hardcodes Scotch nested dissection for PaStiX. On large tetrahedral
meshes METIS orders with much less fill: the 2.9M-equation periodic box of the
semicrystal RVE has 5.8e9 nonzeros in L with Scotch (46 GB LU in mixed
precision), against 2.2e9 for a METIS ordering of the same pattern.

PASTIX_ORDERING=metis (or METIS) selects PastixOrderMetis; unset or anything
else keeps Scotch, so existing runs are unchanged. PaStiX must be built with
PASTIX_ORDERING_METIS (and a METIS whose idx_t matches pastix_int_t). The
ordering in use is printed once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/ccx_2.23/src/pastix.c
+++ b/ccx_2.23/src/pastix.c
@@ -242,6 +242,19 @@
 	
 	// Set best PaStiX parameters for CalculiX usage
     piparm[IPARM_ORDERING]  				= PastixOrderScotch;
+    {
+        /* PASTIX_ORDERING=metis selects METIS nested dissection (PaStiX built
+           with PASTIX_ORDERING_METIS); default and anything else: Scotch */
+        const char* pastix_ordering = getenv("PASTIX_ORDERING");
+        static int ordering_noted = 0;
+        if( pastix_ordering && (strcmp(pastix_ordering, "metis") == 0 || strcmp(pastix_ordering, "METIS") == 0) ){
+            piparm[IPARM_ORDERING] = PastixOrderMetis;
+        }
+        if( !ordering_noted ){
+            printf(" PaStiX ordering: %s\n", piparm[IPARM_ORDERING] == PastixOrderMetis ? "METIS" : "Scotch");
+            ordering_noted = 1;
+        }
+    }
     if( mode == AS || mode == CP ){
         piparm[IPARM_SCHEDULER] 			= PastixSchedStatic;
     }
